PROJECT TYPE

This project is a production restaurant platform and ordering system.

It includes:

- customer ordering
- checkout and payments
- kitchen display system
- admin dashboard
- marketing tools
- loyalty systems
- analytics
- restaurant operations tools


TECHNOLOGY STACK

Frontend

React
TypeScript
Vite

Styling

Tailwind CSS

Backend

Supabase

Payments

Stripe

Hosting

Netlify


CODE STANDARDS

All code must follow strict TypeScript practices.

Do not introduce the "any" type unless absolutely necessary.

Use functional React components only.

Use modern React patterns with hooks.

Avoid class components.

All imports must use the @ alias for src when possible.


PROJECT ARCHITECTURE

The project follows a modular architecture.

src/app
Application boot logic, router, providers, layouts.

src/modules
Core product modules such as orders, checkout, menu.

src/features
Administrative and internal systems.

src/pages
Route entry points used by the router.

src/components
Reusable UI components.


ROUTING RULES

The project uses React Router.

All routes must return a valid component.

Do not create routes that render blank pages.

Large routes should use lazy loading.

Admin routes must require authentication.

Role protected routes must use RoleGuard.

Authentication protected routes must use AuthGuard.

Do not modify router architecture without explicit instruction.


AUTHENTICATION

Authentication is handled by Supabase.

The application uses role based access control.

Supported roles:

admin
staff
customer

Admin routes must only be accessible by admin users.

Staff routes must only be accessible by admin or staff.


SECURITY RULES

Never expose secrets or API keys in frontend code.

Stripe payment validation must always occur server side.

User data must be protected using Supabase Row Level Security.

Admin functionality must always require authentication checks.

Never bypass authentication guards.


PERFORMANCE RULES

Use lazy loading for large route modules.

Avoid unnecessary component re-renders.

Keep bundle size minimal.

Prefer modular code over monolithic files.


AI BEHAVIOR RULES

Do not perform large refactors without explicit instruction.

Follow the existing architecture patterns.

Do not create duplicate components.

Do not modify critical infrastructure such as router or authentication systems unless explicitly requested.

Prefer extending existing modules rather than creating new patterns.


PRODUCT FOCUS

The system is designed to grow into a restaurant operating platform including:

ordering system
checkout
kitchen display
inventory management
marketing automation
loyalty programs
analytics dashboard
staff management


DEVELOPMENT GOAL

Maintain production quality code.

Maintain strong architecture consistency.

Ensure all features integrate with the existing modular system.

Prioritize security, maintainability, and scalability.